    "Chain responses were replayed from a cache. A live trace waits on the public chain APIs, whose free keys are rate-limited; the limiter shares that limit between workers, so more workers do not make a live trace faster once the limit is reached. Live throughput was not measured.",
    "The case store and the queue are one DuckDB file with one writing process: the pool stores every result itself, one at a time.",
